diff -ruN /tmp/empty/README.md CloudStream-Desktop/README.md
--- /tmp/empty/README.md	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ CloudStream-Desktop/README.md	2026-02-05 00:31:21.561951031 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# CloudStream Desktop
+
+CloudStream Desktop is a Windows‐native client for streaming media using the
+same provider ecosystem as the CloudStream Android application.  It
+implements the core functionality of the Android app—including modular
+providers, streaming via libmpv and persistent bookmarks and history—in a
+desktop‐friendly WPF application.
+
+## Features
+
+* **Home** page with continue watching and bookmarks sections.
+* **Search** across all installed providers with instant navigation to
+  playback.
+* **Player** page powered by mpv with support for headers, multiple
+  qualities, subtitles and resume playback.
+* **Extensions** manager listing all loaded providers from the `Plugins`
+  directory.
+* **Settings** page with dark theme toggle and the ability to clear watch
+  history.
+* **SQLite persistence** for bookmarks, history and resume positions.
+
+## Building
+
+To build and run the application you will need a recent .NET SDK (e.g.
+version 8.0 or higher) and the Windows desktop development workload
+installed.
+
+Clone the repository and restore the NuGet packages:
+
+```sh
+git clone https://github.com/donatelloroberto/CloudStream-Desktop.git
+cd CloudStream-Desktop
+dotnet build
+```
+
+The project targets `net8.0-windows` and uses WPF.  After building, you
+can run the application either from your IDE or by executing:
+
+```sh
+dotnet run --project CloudStream.Desktop.csproj
+```
+
+## Installing Extensions
+
+Providers are loaded from the `Plugins` directory located alongside the
+executable.  To install an extension, drop the compiled plugin DLL into
+the `Plugins` folder and restart the application.  Each plugin must
+implement the `CloudStream.Desktop.Plugins.IProvider` interface.
+
+## Data Location
+
+Application data (SQLite database) is stored in the local application
+data folder under `CloudStream/cloudstream.db`.  Clearing history via
+the settings page will remove watch history but leave bookmarks intact.
